<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agordat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Akordat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agordat is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> on the Barka River. Italian forces defeated the Mahdists of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> there in 1890 and 1893, and the Italian railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asmara">Asmara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keren">Keren</a> was extended to it in the 1920s. It was the scene of fighting between British and Italian forces in early 1941.</p></div>
